# Commit messages (GUI "Generate Commit Message" and Agent)

When generating a Git commit message for this repository, use Conventional Commits:

- Format: `<type>(<scope>): <summary>` (scope optional)
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `perf`, `refactor`, `style`, `docs`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`
- Summary: imperative mood, max 72 characters, no trailing period
- Body only when the change is non-obvious; explain why, not what; prefer no body
- Breaking change: `!` before the colon and a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer
- One logical change per message; do not restate the diff line by line
- Match English subject lines as in recent Conventional Commits in this repo
